WEBVTT

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.590
<i>At long last, the diabolical 
proposal is complete...</i>

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.590
<i>for Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.220
It's Tonegawa, sir. I'm coming in.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.890
<b>Bored...!</b>

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.450
Bored...

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.410
This is dull.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.290
I'm fed up.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:34.180
They prattle on about "likes" and 
"friends" and "offline meet-ups."

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.010
Who they "follow," and who they 
"DM," and what they "retweet."

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.520
It's asinine. Every bit of it.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.190
Wouldn't you agree,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.020
Tonegawa?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.860
Yes, sir, you're absolutely correct.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:57.390
Actually, President, regarding the 
diabolical project you tasked me with...

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.620
<i>There is no better moment to 
turn in the project proposal!</i>

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.750
I have the complete proposal ready for your—

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.530
Movies.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.410
I want to see a movie.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:12.390
A movie that can actually entertain me.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.400
<b>Movie</b>

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.510
<i>No... Tonegawa holds back.</i>

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.170
Sir, you like movies?

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.840
Of course not.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.170
Most movies are tedious drivel...

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.310
A way of killing time that barely 
ranks above doing nothing at all.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.400
Right...

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.870
But... not all of them.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.870
They're incredibly rare, 
but some of them are worth watching.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.660
And those are actually capable 
of amusing me, if only a bit.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.400
For instance, Hitchcock's works, 
or Kurokawa Akira.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.300
You mean Kurosawa Akira, sir?

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.520
What difference does it make?!

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.260
I'm sorry, sir!

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.010
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.610
<i>What the hell am I doing?!</i>

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.610
<i>I thought he was going to tell me to show him 
the Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors proposal!</i>

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.420
<i>I just don't understand...</i>

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.370
<i>After all my years at Teiai, the president's 
mood swings are still beyond me!</i>

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.870
<i>And so, several minutes later...</i>

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.170
<i>It's finally at the climax.</i>

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.290
<i>He's asleep?!</i>

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.890
<i>Should I wake him?</i>

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.370
<i>No... If I wake him when 
he's so sound asleep...</i>

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.760
<i>The story is in the middle 
of an explosive climax!</i>

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.910
<i>But if I don't wake him, 
he'll demand to know why I didn't!</i>

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.410
<i>I know it!</i>

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.700
<i>If I wake him or if I don't, 
I'm in for hell either way!</i>

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:19.210
<i>Damned if you do, damned if you don't. 
A decision that brings only dread!</i>

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.340
<i>No! Wait!</i>

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:22.660
Hey!

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.720
Stop the film until the president wakes up.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.600
Yes, sir.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.980
<i>Now I won't have to wake him up 
or worry about him missing the climax.</i>

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:41.410
<i>In what seemed like a 
crisis with no solution,</i>

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.450
<i>he finds an answer to both problems!</i>

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.590
<i>Now I just need to wait.</i>

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.660
<i>Until the president wakes up on his own...</i>

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.300
<i>Thus, an hour passes.</i>

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:08.200
<i>He's still fast asleep... 
He must be really tired.</i>

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.060
<i>And then, another thirty minutes later...</i>

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.520
You have the nerve to snore like some 
kind of oaf when I'm right here?!

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.120
Uh, sir, I—

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.450
Plus, you missed out on 
that emotional climax!

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.870
What kind of fool are you?!

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.500
Take your punishment!

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.720
I'm going to bed.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.840
<i>Tonegawa blew it!</i>

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.730
<i>His major mistake leaves him unable</i>

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:44.410
<i>to turn in the project proposal for 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:49.110
<i>But I'm tired from working so hard, too!</i>

00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:01.030
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:01.030
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.440
<i>Tonegawa has five days until the deadline 
to turn in the project proposal.</i>

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.240
Agenda 03
<b>Soul-Searching</b>

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.200
<i>Five days should be plenty of time</i>

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:34.450
<b>Project Proposal
Tei</b>

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.480
<i>to find the right timing to turn this in.</i>

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.450
<i>Some kind of perfect opportunity...</i>

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:38.580
Tonegawa-sensei! He's leaving!

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.000
Tomorrow!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.520
The president's going to 
be in Hawaii for ten days!

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.410
H-Hawaii?!

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.880
Yes, sir! So it has to be today!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.010
You have to turn in the proposal today!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.800
<i>Psst...</i>

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.610
<i>Impossible... Why?! Why would he 
go to Hawaii now, of all times?!</i>

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.900
<i>The Don of Teiai, Hyoudou Kazutaka, 
enjoys his freedom!</i>

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.270
Let's go turn it in right away!

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.680
If we go now—

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.280
No!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.650
I can't. Even knowing that, I can't just...

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.860
But, sir...

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:18.790
Think of how it'll play out if I 
turn it in when he's in a bad mood.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:31.050
He'll reject the proposal on a whim! 
That could be the cruel fate that awaits us!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.320
If that happens, we're done for!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:40.810
<b>Project Proposal
Tei</b>

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.320
Even if our time runs out today, 
there's no point in rushing

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.810
to turn it in if it's going to be rejected!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.690
Th-Then when are you going to turn it in?

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.110
Well...

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:52.100
Yamazaki, before you were assigned 
to my team, didn't you...

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:56.560
Oh, right. I was working 
directly for President Hyoudou.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:58.760
Does anything come to mind?

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.920
The ideal timing to deal with the 
president, when he's in a good mood!

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.840
It's hard to say when he's in a good mood...

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.760
The president is almost always in a bad mood.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.470
It's like his default state is a bad mood.... 
He was probably born in a bad mood.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:21.480
Plus, he's a tyrant, and his mood swings 
are intense, so he's impossible to predict.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:26.550
So if I had to name a time when he 
might be in a relatively good mood...

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.020
What is it?

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:31.560
There's one.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.700
For just a short time.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.810
<i>Psst...</i>

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.700
It's a tight window,

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.080
but a golden time does exist where the 
president is typically in a good mood!

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.750
When is it, Yamazaki?!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.710
<i>And so...</i>

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.070
<i>That same day, at 9 PM,</i>

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:56.970
<b>King's Bath</b>

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:56.970
<i>in front of the Teiai home office's private 
bath for the president: The King's Bath!</i>

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:58.970
<i>Okay...</i>

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.210
<i>Looks like he should be bathing right now.</i>

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:05.730
<i>He'll probably be coming 
out in just a few minutes.</i>

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.260
<i>That'll be my moment to strike.</i>

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.410
The best time to approach the president

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:12.860
is when he's fresh out of the bath.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:13.970
The bath?

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:17.350
Yes, sir. This is pretty well-known 
among the men in black

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:18.870
who work directly under him.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:22.360
The president really loves his bath time!

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.360
Even though he's almost always in a bad mood,

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.000
he'll generally be pretty mellow 
after getting out of the bath.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.090
But it's only for a short time.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:37.490
Once he walks the short distance 
to his private room, you're out!

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:41.510
After bathing, he always 
heads straight to his room.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.270
You only have a moment!

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.680
<i>A moment of only twenty seconds in which</i>

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.720
<i>his body is still warmed, 
his aura still steaming...</i>

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.000
<i>A brief flash of golden time!</i>

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.660
I-If I may...

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:58.690
How do you know he's usually in a good 
mood after getting out of the bath?

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:02.030
Oh, from the angle of his eyebrows.

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.000
The angle of his eyebrows?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.790
Yes. It's pretty common knowledge among 
those of us working under the president...

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:14.580
You can usually get a good read on 
his mood by the angle of his eyebrows.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:20.970
From zero to forty degrees, you're 
usually good to go. That's still safe.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:26.560
But if they arch higher than forty 
degrees, that's the red zone!

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:33.060
Of course, this rule isn't totally infallible. 
Sometimes there are exceptions.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:38.370
But we generally used this 
method to gauge his mood.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:43.320
A-Amazing! Yamazaki-san, going to him 
after his bath might really work!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:47.450
I'd still say there's only a 50/50 chance.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.830
No, maybe even less than that.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.250
You can call it the best time,

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.850
but all that really means is it's possible 
he'll be in a relatively better mood.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:00.840
I've seen plenty of times when he was 
angry after getting out of the bath, too.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:06.060
That being the case, Tonegawa-sensei, 
even if the president looks totally normal

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.350
when you approach him after bath time,

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.230
make sure to check first.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.480
Check the angle of his eyebrows!

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:22.410
And if the angle is any higher 
than 40 degrees, give up!

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:29.160
It's not much of a chance, but it's the
best one you have, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:32.250
<i>Indeed, it's not much of a chance.</i>

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.750
<b>King's Bath</b>

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:37.110
<i>Nothing about what Yamazaki 
mentioned is a sure deal.</i>

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.380
<i>It's all within the realm of speculation,</i>

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.380
<b>Project Proposal
Tei</b>

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.990
<i>but it'll do.</i>

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:43.390
<i>The way things are now...</i>

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.410
<i>No, it's more like I don't have any choice!</i>

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:52.390
<i>Even if I'm grasping at a spider's web 
that might blow away with a breeze!</i>

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.570
<i>Psst...</i>

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:57.770
There he is!

00:11:58.450 --> 00:11:59.860
The president!

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.440
<i>The moment has arrived! 
Judgment is upon him!</i>

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:05.370
<i>Live or die, the time is now!</i>

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:08.490
<i>Well?</i>

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:11.250
<i>The angle...</i>

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.120
<i>The eyebrows!</i>

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.540
<i>He bears witness!</i>

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.630
<i>Impossible! Why would he 
be wearing a face mask?!</i>

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:37.430
<i>Now I can't tell the angle of 
his eyebrows, or anything else!</i>

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:42.030
<i>At this moment, the year had 
already passed into late October.</i>

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:45.950
<i>The seasons were changing, 
with the air getting more dry.</i>

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:51.410
<i>A time when the elderly start to
get concerned about their skin!</i>

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.340
<i>And even if he is the king of the Teiai Group,</i>

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:58.920
<i>Hyoudou Kazutaka is one 
other thing: an old man!</i>

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.170
<i>And even royalty needs skin care!</i>

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:25.290
<i>Tonegawa is once again unable 
to turn in the proposal!</i>

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.850
Punishment!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.020
<i>Failure.</i>

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:41.040
<i>Tonegawa was unable to submit the proposal, 
with the deadline only five days away.</i>

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.040
<b>Project Proposal
Tei</b>

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:44.110
<i>And not only that, but the chance is gone</i>

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:47.800
<i>because the president is now on 
vacation in Hawaii for ten days!</i>

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.600
<b>Three Days Later</b>

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:59.600
<i>Now, three days later,</i>

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.920
<i>in Meeting Room 3...</i>

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.240
And so, I went to Hawaii, as well.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.930
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:12.650
This was, of course, to turn in 
the proposal to the president.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.990
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.000
<i>Tonegawa-sensei...</i>

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:18.000
As a result...

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.420
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:21.920
It was approved!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:25.670
We've got the full go-ahead for 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.170
Yes!

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:36.740
When I saw the president in Hawaii, 
he was in a better mood than I expected.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.810
I even confirmed the angle of his eyebrows.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:51.590
Come in.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:00.470
Tonegawa-sensei?

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.410
What's this?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.210
<i>Psst...</i>

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.630
We finally managed to get 
our project approved.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:10.050
It'd be a waste to move on to the next step

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.370
without celebrating a bit, don't you think?

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:17.010
That being the case, today, we're going 
to have a party here in the meeting room.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.530
Cheers!

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.740
<i>This is a time when taking 
immediate action would help</i>

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.740
<i>ensure the success of the project...</i>

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:33.740
<i>But that's exactly why we 
should relax while we can.</i>

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:37.740
<i>With work only getting 
harder from this point on,</i>

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.250
<i>it's important to release some of 
the stress that's been building.</i>

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.650
<i>Give them a fresh start!</i>

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:50.100
<i>Plus, holding it in the same meeting room 
we always use was clever, even for me.</i>

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:55.210
<i>There's no better venue I could've used for 
the team to grow closer and more united.</i>

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.090
<i>Tonegawa is certain!</i>

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:01.890
<i>That he has a complete grasp of his men, 
and that their bonds will deepen!</i>

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:05.030
Yamazaki, you saved me this time.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.270
It was nothing, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:09.920
Here, let me pour you one, Kawasaki.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:10.900
Thank you!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.760
You drinking, Hagio?

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:13.500
Definitely!

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.970
You have to try this, Ogino!

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.410
Thanks, sir!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:22.260
That was perfect, Sensei. You have 
all of our names and faces figured out!

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:23.930
Naturally.

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:25.420
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.520
Are you doing anything after this?

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:28.800
Nakata, don't tell me...

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.290
You guys are going bowling?

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:35.930
I'm sure some of you know this, 
but my best score is 192.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.580
Aw, I'm not gonna lose today, though!

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:39.970
Come on, join us!

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.010
All right, then.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:47.830
Just don't forget, we've got another 
meeting at nine tomorrow morning.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.320
So don't go too wild.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:50.800
Right!

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:54.100
<i>And so the joyous festivities continued!</i>

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.450
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.450
<i>Then, the following morning,</i>

00:16:58.100 --> 00:16:59.890
<i>in Meeting Room 3...</i>

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:18.390
<i>The current time is 9:22:10 AM.</i>

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:26.230
<i>I'm not wrong about the 
time, then. Which means...</i>

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.050
Hello?

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.420
<i>I-I'm so sorry, sir!</i>

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:36.550
<i>The thing is, after you left, 
we were all really worked up...</i>

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.360
<i>and before we realized it, it was morning!</i>

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.670
<i>We're all on our way to the office—</i>

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:41.540
Forget it.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.830
Don't bother coming in today!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.570
<i>Tonegawa-sen—</i>

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.710
<i>Tonegawa is furious!</i>

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:54.960
<i>He returns to his desk and prepares to 
head home, upset over this loss of time!</i>

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:58.070
<i>Idiots. Just keep goofing around...</i>

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:01.860
<i>And keep losing more valuable opportunities.</i>

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:08.390
We're so sorry, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.750
Even children can say "I'm sorry."

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:17.200
Society expects you to apologize.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:21.300
The important thing is how you demonstrate 
that you actually want to make up for it.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.460
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:32.090
<i>At that moment, Tonegawa feels an 
eerie chill, an ominous premonition...</i>

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:36.710
We thought you would say 
just that, Tonegawa-sensei.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:37.840
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:40.360
<i>Who is this?!</i>

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:44.550
We've all done some serious 
soul-searching over this one.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:45.350
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.900
They look the same!

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:50.390
<i>Tonegawa has just realized the 
nature of his bad feeling!</i>

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:54.090
We couldn't face you without doing something.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:54.980
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:56.970
<i>So does he!</i>

00:18:57.460 --> 00:19:01.560
So we thought about what we should do.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:02.240
<i>Psst...</i>

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.690
And what we could do to 
make our remorse tangible.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:06.450
<i>Psst...</i>

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:07.950
Don't tell me...

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.710
You all...

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:13.860
<i>And then he realizes the exact 
reason they all look the same!</i>

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:19.220
Yes, sir! We've shaved our heads!

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:25.450
Of course, these haircuts aren't 
just about our appearance,

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.470
but to demonstrate how we'll make up 
for what we've done by working hard...

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:32.230
I see. Looks like I was right about you all.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:34.470
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:36.610
You men are truly...

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.440
complete morons!

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:45.200
The one thing that was helping me 
distinguish between your sorry faces

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.200
was your hairstyles!

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:51.270
And now, the men who wear the same 
suits, with the same sunglasses,

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:54.830
all have the same damn haircut?!

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:58.210
You're impossible to tell apart! 
It can't be done!

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.720
It's like I'm in the Matrix!

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.580
Matrix?

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:08.370
You know what he means?

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:09.430
No.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.980
Idiots! Watch the damn <i>Matrix</i>!

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:15.560
Sorry, sir.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.070
Well, we can do a team 
screening tomorrow morning...

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:18.730
Idiots!

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.300
You're all so stupid! Imbeciles!

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.750
How did we even get on this topic?!

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:23.880
That's why I told them...

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:27.990
This wouldn't be enough to satisfy you.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:28.870
Kikuchi!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:34.110
If we're truly sorry for our 
actions, then we should go...

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:37.380
further, to the ultimate edge,

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.130
all the way to the surface!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.650
Idiot!

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:46.490
<i>And so, the names of the men in black he 
worked so hard to remember are all rewritten!</i>

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:48.140
<i>Back to zero!</i>

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:52.570
<i>Tonegawa now finds himself reloaded!</i>

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.640
<i>A completely unexpected pratfall!</i>

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:59.940
<i>But, regardless, hang in there, Tonegawa!</i>

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.400
<i>Don't give up, Tonegawa!</i>

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:10.780
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer,</i>

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:15.130
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:19.920
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:57.700
Next time: Self-Destruct.

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Self-Destruct</b>
